Article 44 Annual Reporting

Legal persons and organizations must report annually to the Ministry of Technology and Communications regarding the status and implementation of cybersecurity work within the month of January of every year. The annual report comprises the following content:

1. Cybersecurity measures that have been implemented;

2. Incidents or cybersecurity threats that have occurred and methods of remediation;

3. Compliance in the implementation of the cybersecurity plan;

4. Computer system vulnerabilities that have been found and methods of remediation;

5. Awareness raising and cybersecurity training;

6. Establishment of a plan for the following year.

The Ministry of Technology and Communications must compile, analyze and report results to the Government within a period of thirty days.

Article 45 Exchange of Information Between Countries

The exchange of information between countries regarding cybersecurity shall be as follows:

1. Information regarding threats and vulnerabilities of computer systems;

