AGREEMENT ON CONDUCTING INTERNET SERVICE BUSINESS OPERATIONS, Art. 23 | p.12

To the staff of the Department of Technology and Communications and the responsible authorities that are involved in monitoring and inspecting business operations:

Guarantee, comply with the principles, conditions and standards that are defined in Article 4, Article 12, Article 17, Article 21, Article 22 and Article 23 of this agreement;

Provide information and connection details completely and accurately to the Department of Technology and Communications on a quarterly basis or according to notification in each case;

Keep the data of service users confidential and secure, except in cases where there is an order from the competent authority;

Record and maintain data on the history of use of Internet service users for a minimum of 01 year;

Provide information and news about various services to service users on a regular basis, clearly and precisely;

Guarantee service quality, fair competition and fair pricing according to the law and regulations that are defined;

Resolve problems and technical disputes for service users in accordance with procedures;

Have a plan to restore telecommunications and Internet networks in case of disaster, crisis, emergency and in case of network failure;

Have uniforms, signs or insignia and the name of the company clearly and precisely for staff installing and equipping telecommunications and Internet equipment;

Print the trademark/insignia of the Internet service provider on the outside of the telecommunications and Internet equipment clearly throughout the service life;

Collect telecommunications and Internet equipment that is no longer in use for orderliness and organization, guarantee safety to life, property without causing impact to society and the environment;

Submit information reports on their service operations such as: use of telecommunications resources, technical security and connections to the Department of Technology and Communications on a regular basis.

